.TH QUICKSHELL 1 "2026-05-04" "quickshell 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quickshell \- flexible QtQuick-based desktop shell toolkit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quickshell
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fISUBCOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quickshell is a toolkit for building status bars, widgets, lockscreens,
and other desktop components using Qt6 and QtQuick. It supports both
Wayland and X11, with integrations for PipeWire, MPRIS, system tray,
PAM, Bluetooth, and compositor-specific features for Hyprland and
Sway/i3. Configuration is done declaratively in QML with live
hot-reloading.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help message and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print quickshell's version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-no\-duplicate
Exit immediately if another instance of the given config is running.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Detach from the controlling terminal.
.SS "Config Selection"
Quickshell detects configurations as named directories under each XDG config
directory as \fI<xdg dir>/quickshell/<config name>/shell.qml\fR.
.PP
If \fI<xdg dir>/quickshell/shell.qml\fR exists, it will be registered as
the \(aqdefault\(aq configuration, and no subdirectories will be considered.
If \fB\-\-config\fR is not passed, \(aqdefault\(aq will be assumed.
.PP
Alternatively, a config can be selected by path with \fB\-\-path\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-path " " \fITEXT\fR
Path to a QML file or config folder. Excludes \fB\-\-config\fR and
\fB\-\-manifest\fR. Environment variable: \fBQS_CONFIG_PATH\fR.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fITEXT\fR
Name of a quickshell configuration to run. Excludes \fB\-\-path\fR.
Environment variable: \fBQS_CONFIG_NAME\fR.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-manifest " " \fITEXT\fR
[DEPRECATED] Path to a quickshell manifest. Excludes \fB\-\-path\fR.
Environment variable: \fBQS_MANIFEST\fR.
.SS Logging
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disables colored logging. Can also be disabled by setting the
\fBNO_COLOR\fR environment variable.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-times
Log timestamps with each message.
.TP
.BI \-\-log\-rules " TEXT"
Log rules to apply, in the format of QT_LOGGING_RULES.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Increases log verbosity. \fB\-v\fR shows INFO level internal logs.
\fB\-vv\fR shows DEBUG level internal logs.
.SS Debugging
.TP
.BI \-\-debug " PORT"
Open the given port (0\-65535) for a QML debugger connection.
.TP
.B \-\-waitfordebug
Wait for a QML debugger to connect before executing the configuration.
Requires \fB\-\-debug\fR.
.SS "Subcommand Filtering"
Subcommands that operate on running instances accept the following filter:
.TP
.B \-\-any\-display
Do not restrict the match to instances launched on the current display.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B log
Print quickshell logs.
.TP
.B list
List running quickshell instances.
.TP
.B kill
Kill quickshell instances.
.TP
.B ipc
Communicate with other Quickshell instances. Includes per-handler
listener subcommands for IpcHandler signals registered by the running
shell.
.TP
.B msg
[DEPRECATED] Moved to \fBipc call\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Run the default configuration:
.B qs
.TP
Run a named configuration:
.B qs \-c myconfig
.TP
Run from a specific path:
.B qs \-p ~/myshell
.TP
Run a specific QML file:
.B qs \-p ~/myshell/randomfile.qml
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B QS_CONFIG_PATH
Path to a QML file or config folder.
.TP
.B QS_CONFIG_NAME
Name of a quickshell configuration to run.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
If set to a non-empty value, disables colored logging.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR qs (1)
